### Orders API: ready-to-run requests
### Open in IntelliJ IDEA (HTTP Client) or VS Code (REST Client extension) after `docker compose up`.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### 1. Register a customer (returns accessToken)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "fullName": "Jane Doe"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 2. Search products (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?q=keyboard&page=0&size=10

### 3. Place an order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": 1, "quantity": 2 },
    { "productId": 2, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.id); %}

### 4. List my orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Cancel the order (stock is returned)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Log in as the demo admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "change-me-please"
}

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 7. Create a product (admin only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "CAM-4K",
  "name": "4K Webcam",
  "description": "Auto-focus, dual microphones",
  "price": 79.00,
  "stock": 25
}
